{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"0e9d9e61-374e-4315-9be2-f89b97540405","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Before implementing the fix, I consulted the Worklore MCP server (`suggest_for_project` and `get_story`) which identified the relevant story:\n`2026-04-24-two-cache-control-segments-so-agent-memory-writes-don-t-evic` (\"Two cache_control segments so agent memory writes don't evict the whole Claude system prompt\").\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Split the System Prompt into Two Cache Control Segments in [`bot.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-S9GpNG/bot.py#L130-L138)**:\n   - Previously, [`build_system()`](file:///private/tmp/h-S9GpNG/bot.py#L130-L138) combined the static coaching instructions (`INSTRUCTIONS`) and volatile athlete memory (`athlete_context`) into a single block with a single `cache_control` marker. Because Anthropic prompt caching hashes sequentially from the start of the prompt prefix, appending a memory fact invalidated the entire block.\n   - Refactored [`build_system()`](file:///private/tmp/h-S9GpNG/bot.py#L130-L138) to return two separate text blocks, each with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n     - **Block 1**: Static instructions (`INSTRUCTIONS.strip()`), invariant across athletes and sessions.\n     - **Block 2**: Volatile athlete context (`athlete_context(a, today)`), containing the date, profile, zones, and dynamic facts.\n   - With this change, memory writes from `save_fact` only invalidate and recreate the cache for the dynamic tail block (~240 tokens) while keeping the static instruction block cached.\n\n2. **Documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///private/tmp/h-S9GpNG/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Detailed the root cause, implementation details, and caching behavior.\n","duration_seconds":68.70499,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":119658,"output_tokens":2318,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":261478,"total_tokens":121976}}}
